  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.1 - Requires OSKHelpers 2.1.2. The entropy of the default protector is read and created with CredentialProtector.CreateOrReadEntropyFile, instead of an equivalent copy of the same logic: __mail.entropy, its format and the passwords already encrypted are unchanged.\n2.0.0 - Requires OSKHelpers 2.1.0. New net8.0 target built against MailKit 5; the netstandard2.0 target is built against MailKit 4.16 and accepts MailKit [4.16.0, 5.0.0). SetupSmtp and SetupImap accept an optional CredentialProtector to read passwords encrypted with DPAPI or AES; SmtpPassword and ImapPassword are kept obfuscated in memory with PasswordObfuscator, still encrypted when read encrypted, and decrypted at each read. New Setup<T> for JsonSettings<T> classes implementing ISettingsSmtp/ISettingsImap: encrypts the plain-text passwords and saves the file without a backup copy. Without a protector, the entropy is read from __mail.entropy in Paths.DefaultConfigsDirectory (created on first use). New CheckIniPasswordsProtection and ProtectPassword, to check and encrypt the passwords of an INI file (also with the default protector).\n1.2.5 - Added ISettingsSmtp and ISettingsImap interfaces.",
